From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 06:58:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(video): score the cut plan before paying to render it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The post-render QA gate catches broken output — black picture, silent
audio, truncated encode. It cannot catch boring, because boring encodes
perfectly. A topic video that lands as one still held over the whole
narration passes every existing check and still is not worth publishing.

So judge the scene layout before the encode, while the cut rhythm is
still free to change. planGate.ts scores five dimensions off data the
pipeline already has (scene durations, distinct source clips, narration
cue starts, stills vs footage) and returns a repaired layout plus what it
could not fix.

Order of preference is repair, then warn, then refuse:

- repair: any scene held past 8s is split into equal cuts that rotate
  through the other available clips, preserving total scene time exactly
  so the composition still lines up with the narration
- warn: a cut rate slower than the format allows (5s for stills under a
  Ken Burns move, 9s for real footage), a visual carrying more than four
  spoken sentences, or a slideshow risk at or above 0.5 goes to the job
  log with the reasons ranked worst first
- refuse: only at risk 0.85, which arithmetically needs stills AND a
  single clip AND long holds AND repetition all at once — nothing
  recutting can rescue. The tenant is refunded through the existing
  VideoGenProviderError path.

The gate scores the layout the composer will actually render, not the raw
one: composeTopicVideo diversifies adjacent repeats itself, so scoring
before that would flag an already-fixed problem.

Slideshow rendering is deliberately not gated — a user who uploaded their
own photos must not be told their slideshow is too much like a slideshow.

Concepts read from OpenMontage (AGPLv3); no code, prompts, or thresholds
copied — every weight and ceiling here is written for this pipeline.

